["<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5c15a0d067c37a4e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01HxFnurCsJh4Vwkq9B4yqi3</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/a5c15a0d067c37a4e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement progression milestone M0\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>M0 and M1 are both done and committed on `feature/progression-m0`, in the worktree only; nothing is merged to main. All four gates passed.\n\n## Commits\n- `060be9d`: M0. The 19 existing talents are rewritten in the new tree model and behave the same as before.\n- `84acf7a`: M1. The player and the companion each have their own points, the save file has a party section, and old saves migrate.\n- `39d9a35`: a short note in `docs/proposals/progression-unified.md` §5.4 correcting the pacing with the measured bond XP.\n\n## Gates\n1. **EditMode tests:** after M0, 1202 of 1202 passed (the 798 existing ones plus 404 new). After M1, 1215 of 1215 passed. Both ran in the scratch copy `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/pm0-copy`, with the art folders copied in from the main checkout.\n2. **Identity test:** `unity/Assets/Tests/Editor/LegacyTalents.cs` is a frozen copy of the old talent rules. `TalentModelEquivalenceTests` runs the old and new code side by side over seeded random buy, refund and respec sequences, corrupted saves, and the bot's buying order. It checks that both give the same answers, refunds, saved list (including order), validity, and exactly the same final value for every stat on the player and the companion. After M1 the test compares each character with the old rules limited to that character's branches.\n3. **Bot:**\n   - On main and on M0, the bot finished 3 runs with 3 wins. The `[TALENT]` lines were byte-for-byte identical; both runs happened to clear the same rooms and win the same runs, since the bot has no seed.\n   - On M1, the bot also finished 3 runs with 3 wins. The log shows two `[TREE]` point ledgers with no shared keys.\n   - Every run had only the known SearchDatabase ArgumentOutOfRange error. M1 had 5 \"timeScale is flapping\" warnings against 3 on main. That warning existed before these changes and its count depends on gameplay.\n4. **Bond XP per run:** about **90**, not the 130 the proposal assumed. The six measured runs gave 96, 91, 89 (main) and 87, 87, 93 (M1). The bot won every run, so this includes the win bonus; a lost run should give about 55 by the rules, but that is not measured. As a result the companion's first keystone comes around run 5 if every run is won. At about a 40% win rate, reaching the 20-point cap takes about 30 runs rather than 17.\n\n## Decisions to review\n- **Talents are kept through the migration, not refunded.** The proposal (§3.5) says refund everything, but its reason is the M3 content rework, which hasn't happened yet. A character who can't afford their old talents is refunded on their own.\n- **All old points go to the player.** The old starting point becomes the player's `start:1` key and the rest become `legacy:1..n` keys, so returning players only gain points. The companion's points are rebuilt from its bond level only, not from past wins.\n- **Benched companions:** I followed the recommendation in §8: half of the per-run bond XP (10), no combat XP, no boss points. There is only one companion today, so this rule is covered by tests only. When a second companion arrives (M5), the Growth feature will need to track XP per companion; until then the active companion's XP is copied from Growth's counter.\n- **Talent ranks are still in the model.** Dropping ranks (§3.1) waits for the M3 content.\n- **Smaller changes:**\n  - Stat sources are now named `talent:&lt;tree&gt;:&lt;node&gt;`, so the C-key stats sheet shows \"天赋·knight:vigor\".\n  - `Growth.CompanionMods` is still there; it wasn't in the M1 scope you gave.\n\n## Unverified\n- **Screen layout:** I didn't change it to tabs. It keeps the four columns, shows both point pools in the header, and the R reset applies to the character who owns the selected column. I haven't seen it in a real window, and the `TalentShot` screenshots were not taken.\n- **Bot gaps:** the bot never loses, never abandons a run from the pause menu, and never loads an old save, so those paths are covered by EditMode tests only.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>305462</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>300228</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
